The method uses a hash set `visited` to keep track of the n-tersections that have been visited, and a queue `queue` to store the n-tersections to be visited next. The method starts by adding the starting n-tersection to the queue. It then iterates through the queue, and for each n-tersection, it checks if it is the ending n-tersection. If it is, the method returns "can be travelled".

If it is not the ending n-tersection, the method iterates through the paths for each adjacent n-tersection and adds the next n-tersection to the queue if it has not been visited before. The method continues this process until the queue is empty, at which point, the method returns "cannot be travelled" because there is no path from the starting n-tersection to the ending n-tersection.

