public static int minPerfectSquareSum(int n) {
    int[] dp = new int[n + 1];
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        dp[i] = i;
        for (int j = 1; j * j <= i; j++) {
            dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i], dp[i - j * j] + 1);
        }
    }
    return dp[n];
}
```
Please note that the above code is a solution to the LeetCode problem [Perfect Squares](https://leetcode.com/problems/perfect-squares/) (#279). The problem statement is slightly different, but the solution can be adapted to this problem by changing the return type to `int` and adding a parameter to accept the input integer `n`.

